@doc smysl/0.1 {
  id: v/f9
  intent: incident-brief
  lang: en
  requires: ["smysl.kernel/0.1"]
  granularity: { profile: default }
  roots: [c/regression]
}

# A store written by a later version, read by this one. Nothing here is exotic on
# purpose: the point is that an unfamiliar type is carried rather than refused, and
# that a reader is told so rather than left to assume it saw everything.

@evidence e/latency { status: measured, source: { kind: metric, ref: "auth.p95", captured: 2026-07-22 } }
~ p95 on the auth path rose from 180 ms to 540 ms over four hours.

@claim c/regression { status: derived, grounds: [e/latency] }
~ The 4.2 rollout regressed auth latency.

// `postmortem` is not a kernel type this build knows. A later version added it, and
// this document has to survive the trip: preserved verbatim, reported as SMY-W010,
// re-emitted byte for byte.
@postmortem pm/incident-92 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: "postmortems/92" } }
~ The written record of incident 92, filed the following morning.

@rel pm/incident-92 --elaborates--> c/regression
